{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"boundary","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A startup failure can remove the token-file read denial while workers are still active, allowing a sandbox policy created in that short interval to omit the protection."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Enabling token enforcement with an accepted plain-HTTP proxy configuration leaves ordinary browser users unable to retain the required Secure session cookie and access the UI."}]}